Subject: Rebuild the background palette pair table only when the palette it was built from changes

A speed fix, not an accuracy one. RefreshLine rebuilt its 256-entry table on
every call, and FCEUPPU_LineUpdate calls it on every $2002 read, so a game
polling $2002 for a sprite-zero hit, as Zelda II's title screen does about
1,900 times a frame, spent most of its frame rebuilding a table that had not
changed. Measured with gprof on the PC build: RefreshLine was 72 percent of
the intro's time, and the intro's frame went from 327 to about 148 us.
The table built is the same as before, so every checksum is unchanged:
tools/accuracycoin.py --expect tests/accuracycoin_expected.txt shows no
change, and Castlevania, Zelda, Zelda II and Chip 'n Dale match.

License: GPL-2.0-or-later, as the FCEUmm code it changes (patches/fceumm/README.md).

---
diff --git a/src/ppu.c b/src/ppu.c
index b2fcb29..fa12f36 100644
--- a/src/ppu.c
+++ b/src/ppu.c
@@ -182,9 +182,22 @@ uint8_t UPALRAM[0x03];/* for 0x4/0x8/0xC addresses in palette, the ones in
  *       that hits Pal[0x04/0x08/0x0C] (e.g. Mega Man 3 sprites). */
 static uint16_t fceu_bg_pair_lut[256];
 
+/* The table depends on PALRAM[0x00..0x0F] alone, so it is rebuilt only when
+ * those 16 bytes, priority bits included, differ from the ones it was last
+ * built from.  A game that polls $2002 in a loop calls RefreshLine once per
+ * read, nearly 1,900 times a frame in Zelda II's title screen, and rebuilding
+ * 256 entries each time was most of the frame; the table is the same either
+ * way. */
+static uint8_t fceu_bg_pair_lut_from[16];
+static int fceu_bg_pair_lut_valid;
+
 static void FCEU_BuildBgPairLUT(void)
 {
 	int b;
+	if (fceu_bg_pair_lut_valid && !memcmp(fceu_bg_pair_lut_from, PALRAM, 16))
+		return;
+	memcpy(fceu_bg_pair_lut_from, PALRAM, 16);
+	fceu_bg_pair_lut_valid = 1;
 	for (b = 0; b < 256; b++)
 	{
 #ifdef MSB_FIRST
